{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UUdv8nAZBXWaikuWfi6tkN","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, the type of the cluster ID field in the new metadata record used to persist cluster ID in the log, in KIP-1262 (the proposal to let brokers and observer controllers skip storage formatting before startup), is **String**.\\\\n\\\\nThis is documented in `/store/kips-and-discussions.md` at lines 2584-2588, where Kevin Wu (the KIP proposer) addresses Jun Rao's question about the **ClusterIdRecord Field Type**:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"Current implementation allows String for backward compatibility, but enforces invariant that cluster ID cannot change once set\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe decision to use `String` type (rather than `UUID`) was made to maintain compatibility with existing non-UUID cluster IDs, while still enforcing the invariant that the cluster ID cannot change once it is set.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"kips-and-discussions.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":25.06,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":1,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":273780,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":39562,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.11583899999999998,\\\"input_tokens\\\":82,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1851}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebfb717d-0372-45c0-aea5-caa0c3e97290","uuid":"41bcce3b-77ba-4eb6-9efa-a22b83ee3011","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:32:19.995Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, the type of the cluster ID field in the new metadata record used to persist cluster ID in the log, in KIP-1262 (the proposal to let brokers and observer controllers skip storage formatting before startup), is **String**.\\\\n\\\\nThis is documented in `/store/kips-and-discussions.md` at lines 2584-2588, where Kevin Wu (the KIP proposer) addresses Jun Rao's question about the **ClusterIdRecord Field Type**:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"Current implementation allows String for backward compatibility, but enforces invariant that cluster ID cannot change once set\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe decision to use `String` type (rather than `UUID`) was made to maintain compatibility with existing non-UUID cluster IDs, while still enforcing the invariant that the cluster ID cannot change once it is set.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"kips-and-discussions.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":25.06,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":1,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":273780,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":39562,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.11583899999999998,\\\"input_tokens\\\":82,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1851}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on the context filesystem, the type of the cluster ID field in the new metadata record used to persist cluster ID in the log, in KIP-1262 (the proposal to let brokers and observer controllers skip storage formatting before startup), is **String**.\\n\\nThis is documented in `/store/kips-and-discussions.md` at lines 2584-2588, where Kevin Wu (the KIP proposer) addresses Jun Rao's question about the **ClusterIdRecord Field Type**:\\n\\n> \\\"Current implementation allows String for backward compatibility, but enforces invariant that cluster ID cannot change once set\\\"\\n\\nThe decision to use `String` type (rather than `UUID`) was made to maintain compatibility with existing non-UUID cluster IDs, while still enforcing the invariant that the cluster ID cannot change once it is set.\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"store\",\"README.md\",\"kips-and-discussions.md\"],\"seconds\":25.06,\"truncated\":false,\"turns\":1,\"usage\":{\"cache_read_tokens\":273780,\"cache_write_tokens\":39562,\"cost_usd\":0.11583899999999998,\"input_tokens\":82,\"output_tokens\":1851}}"}}}
